======================================================================
SUMMARY / cross-check against the paper's existing tau~=mgw/2 figure
======================================================================
Paper's stated tau ~= 2.9e-05 N*m implies w ~= 0.2035 m
Old model, governing edge, rigorously computed:  w = 0.3462 m, tau = 4.9334e-05 N*m
New model, governing edge, rigorously computed:  w = 0.3447 m, tau = 4.5446e-05 N*m
Leg geometry (hip radius, thigh/calf lengths, HIP_PITCH/KNEE_BEND) was NOT changed by Phase 2, so the old and new w values above differ only by the CG shift (mass redistribution), not by geometry -- and both are far from the paper's implied ~0.204m regardless. This looks like a pre-existing discrepancy in the paper's own w, independent of the mass redesign -- flagged, not resolved, here.


